cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "highline: when to push the defensive line up (cost, gain and reliability by situation)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Landrevie
    given-names: Julie
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-12-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Julie-Landrevie/highline"
abstract: >-
  Open-source tool that helps a coaching staff read a defensive-line decision
  (push the line up or not) by situation, using SkillCorner Open Data
  (A-League 2024/25, twenty matches of broadcast tracking). Each verdict carries
  the uncertainty of the estimated positions and says what is not established.
  Association only, not causation.
keywords:
  - football analytics
  - tracking data
  - defensive line
  - uncertainty
  - SkillCorner Open Data
  - Analytics Cup 2.0
